IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 9 GENERAL PROVISIONS: s 89 (reconsideration by the Authority and appeal to the Minister) and s 90 (interest on sums unpaid).
-- Seat: the licensee or other person aggrieved by a decision, direction or code: may I ask for reconsideration or appeal, within what time,
-- and must I comply meanwhile.  Time limits are in days after receipt; the facts are the days elapsed.
-- 2000 Revised Edition number: s 90 was s 69A.

§ `s 89 Reconsideration by Authority and appeal to Minister`

-- src:6003 | 89.—(1) Any telecommunication licensee aggrieved by —
-- src:6004 | (a) any decision of the Authority in the exercise of any
-- src:6005 | discretion vested in it by or under this Act; or
-- src:6006 | (b) anything contained in any code of practice or standard of
-- src:6007 | performance or in any direction of the Authority given
-- src:6008 | under section 25, 26(2), 31, 40(2), 41(2), 42(1) or 43(3),
-- src:6009 | may, within 14 days of the receipt of the decision or direction of the
-- src:6010 | Authority or the issue or approval of the code of practice or standard
-- src:6011 | of performance, as the case may be —
-- src:6012 | (c) make a request to the Authority to reconsider the matter; or
-- src:6014 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:6015 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 122
-- src:6017 | (d) appeal to the Minister.
@ref s 89(1) (src:6003-6017)
GIVEN `the person is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority in the exercise of any discretion vested in it by or under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a code of practice or standard of performance, or in a direction of the Authority given under section 25, 26(2), 31, 40(2), 41(2), 42(1) or 43(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the receipt of the decision or direction, or the issue or approval of the code of practice or standard of performance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(1): the licensee may make a request to the Authority to reconsider the matter, or appeal to the Minister` MEANS
        `the person is a telecommunication licensee`
    AND (`the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority in the exercise of any discretion vested in it by or under the Act` OR `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a code of practice or standard of performance, or in a direction of the Authority given under section 25, 26(2), 31, 40(2), 41(2), 42(1) or 43(3)`)
    AND (`days after the receipt of the decision or direction, or the issue or approval of the code of practice or standard of performance` AT MOST 14)

-- src:6021 | (2) Any person (other than a telecommunication licensee) who is
-- src:6022 | aggrieved by —
-- src:6024 | (a) any decision of the Authority under section 5(1), 6, 7(1),
-- src:6025 | 10(1), 17, 23(6), (7) or (12), 27 or 38; or
-- src:6027 | (b) anything contained in any code of practice issued under
-- src:6028 | section 23 or under section 30 read with section 39 or in
-- src:6029 | any direction of the Authority given under section 25,
-- src:6030 | 26(2), 40(2), 41(2), 42(1) or (2),
-- src:6032 | may, within 14 days after the receipt of the decision or direction of the
-- src:6033 | Authority or the issue of the code of practice, as the case may be —
-- src:6035 | (c) make a request to the Authority to reconsider the matter; or
-- src:6037 | (d) appeal to the Minister.
@ref s 89(2) (src:6021-6037)
GIVEN `the person is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority under section 5(1), 6, 7(1), 10(1), 17, 23(6), (7) or (12), 27 or 38` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a code of practice issued under section 23 or under section 30 read with section 39, or in a direction of the Authority given under section 25, 26(2), 40(2), 41(2) or 42(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the receipt of the decision or direction, or the issue of the code of practice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(2): the person may make a request to the Authority to reconsider the matter, or appeal to the Minister` MEANS
        (NOT `the person is a telecommunication licensee`)
    AND (`the person is aggrieved by a decision of the Authority under section 5(1), 6, 7(1), 10(1), 17, 23(6), (7) or (12), 27 or 38` OR `the person is aggrieved by anything contained in a code of practice issued under section 23 or under section 30 read with section 39, or in a direction of the Authority given under section 25, 26(2), 40(2), 41(2) or 42(1) or (2)`)
    AND (`days after the receipt of the decision or direction, or the issue of the code of practice` AT MOST 14)

-- src:6041 | (3) A person must not make both a reconsideration request to the
-- src:6042 | Authority and an appeal to the Minister in respect of the same
-- src:6043 | decision or direction of the Authority or thing contained in a code of
-- src:6044 | practice or standard of performance.
@ref s 89(3) (src:6041-6044)
GIVEN `the person has made a reconsideration request to the Authority about the decision, direction or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made an appeal to the Minister about the same decision, direction or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(3): the person has acted in contravention of the subsection` MEANS
    `the person has made a reconsideration request to the Authority about the decision, direction or thing` AND `the person has made an appeal to the Minister about the same decision, direction or thing`

-- src:6048 | (4) Where a reconsideration request and an appeal have been made
-- src:6049 | in contravention of subsection (3), the appeal is deemed to be
-- src:6050 | withdrawn.
@ref s 89(4) (src:6048-6050)
GIVEN `a reconsideration request and an appeal have been made in contravention of subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(4): the appeal is deemed to be withdrawn` MEANS
    `a reconsideration request and an appeal have been made in contravention of subsection (3)`

-- src:6054 | (5) Where —
-- src:6056 | (a) a reconsideration request has been made to the Authority
-- src:6057 | by any person; and
-- src:6059 | (b) an appeal in respect of the same decision or direction of the
-- src:6060 | Authority or thing contained in a code of practice or
-- src:6061 | standard of performance is made or has been made to the
-- src:6062 | Minister by any other person,
-- src:6064 | the appeal to the Minister is deemed to be withdrawn.
@ref s 89(5) (src:6054-6064)
GIVEN `a reconsideration request has been made to the Authority by a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal about the same decision, direction or thing is made or has been made to the Minister by any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(5): the appeal to the Minister is deemed to be withdrawn` MEANS
    `a reconsideration request has been made to the Authority by a person` AND `an appeal about the same decision, direction or thing is made or has been made to the Minister by any other person`

-- src:6071 | (6) The Authority may determine any reconsideration request under
-- src:6072 | this section by confirming, varying or reversing any decision or
-- src:6073 | direction or by amending any code of practice or standard of
-- src:6074 | performance.
@ref s 89(6) (src:6071-6074)
GIVEN `the Authority determines the reconsideration request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(6): the Authority may determine the request by confirming, varying or reversing the decision or direction, or amending the code of practice or standard of performance` MEANS
    `the Authority determines the reconsideration request`

-- src:6078 | (7) Any telecommunication licensee or any person mentioned in
-- src:6079 | subsection (2) (as the case may be) who is aggrieved by any decision
-- src:6080 | of the Authority under subsection (6) may appeal to the Minister
-- src:6081 | within 14 days after the receipt of the decision.
@ref s 89(7) (src:6078-6081)
GIVEN `the person is a telecommunication licensee or a person mentioned in subsection (2), aggrieved by a decision of the Authority under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days after the receipt of the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(7): the person may appeal to the Minister` MEANS
    `the person is a telecommunication licensee or a person mentioned in subsection (2), aggrieved by a decision of the Authority under subsection (6)` AND (`days after the receipt of the decision` AT MOST 14)

-- src:6085 | (8) Any person who makes an appeal to the Minister under
-- src:6086 | subsection (1), (2) or (7) must within the period specified in that
-- src:6087 | subsection —
-- src:6089 | (a) state as concisely as possible the circumstances under
-- src:6090 | which the appeal arises, and the issues and grounds for the
-- src:6091 | appeal; and
-- src:6093 | (b) submit to the Minister all relevant facts, evidence and
-- src:6094 | arguments for or against the appeal, as the case may be.
@ref s 89(8) (src:6085-6094)
GIVEN `the appellant stated as concisely as possible the circumstances, the issues and the grounds for the appeal, within the period specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant submitted to the Minister all relevant facts, evidence and arguments for or against the appeal, within the period specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(8): the appellant has complied with the subsection` MEANS
    `the appellant stated as concisely as possible the circumstances, the issues and the grounds for the appeal, within the period specified` AND `the appellant submitted to the Minister all relevant facts, evidence and arguments for or against the appeal, within the period specified`

-- src:6098 | (9) The Minister may reject any appeal of an appellant who fails to
-- src:6099 | comply with subsection (8) or (10).
@ref s 89(9) (src:6098-6099)
GIVEN `the appellant fails to comply with subsection (8) or (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(9): the Minister may reject the appeal` MEANS
    `the appellant fails to comply with subsection (8) or (10)`

-- src:6103 | (10) Where an appeal has been made to the Minister under
-- src:6104 | subsection (1), (2) or (7), the Minister may require any person to
-- src:6105 | whom subsection (11) applies to provide the Minister with all such
-- src:6106 | information as the Minister may require for the purpose of
-- src:6107 | considering the appeal and making a determination for resolving it.
-- src:6109 | [10/2005]
-- src:6111 | (11) Subsection (10) applies to —
-- src:6113 | (a) any party to the appeal; and
-- src:6115 | (b) any person who is not a party to the appeal but appears to
-- src:6116 | the Minister to have information that is relevant to the
-- src:6117 | matters mentioned in that subsection.
@ref s 89(10) and (11) (src:6103-6117)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made to the Minister under subsection (1), (2) or (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not a party to the appeal but appears to the Minister to have information relevant to the matters mentioned in subsection (10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(10) and (11): the Minister may require the person to provide the information the Minister requires for considering and determining the appeal` MEANS
    `an appeal has been made to the Minister under subsection (1), (2) or (7)` AND (`the person is a party to the appeal` OR `the person is not a party to the appeal but appears to the Minister to have information relevant to the matters mentioned in subsection (10)`)

-- src:6124 | (12) Any person required to provide information under
-- src:6125 | subsection (10) must provide it in such manner and within such
-- src:6126 | period as may be specified by the Minister.
@ref s 89(12) (src:6124-6126)
GIVEN `the person provides the information in the manner and within the period specified by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(12): the person has complied with the requirement` MEANS
    `the person provides the information in the manner and within the period specified by the Minister`

-- src:6130 | (13) The Minister may determine an appeal under this section by
-- src:6131 | confirming, varying or reversing any decision or direction of the
-- src:6132 | Authority or by amending any code of practice or standard of
-- src:6133 | performance.
@ref s 89(13) (src:6130-6133)
GIVEN `the Minister determines the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(13): the Minister may confirm, vary or reverse the decision or direction, or amend the code of practice or standard of performance` MEANS
    `the Minister determines the appeal`

-- src:6137 | (14) Any decision of the Minister under subsection (13) is final.
@ref s 89(14) (src:6137-6137)
GIVEN `the Minister has made a decision under subsection (13)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(14): the decision of the Minister is final` MEANS
    `the Minister has made a decision under subsection (13)`

-- src:6141 | (15) Unless otherwise provided, where a reconsideration request or
-- src:6142 | an appeal is made under this section, the decision, direction or other
-- src:6143 | matter which requires reconsideration by the Authority or which is
-- src:6144 | appealed against must be complied with until the determination of the
-- src:6145 | reconsideration request or the appeal, as the case may be.
@ref s 89(15) (src:6141-6145)
GIVEN `a reconsideration request or an appeal has been made under section 89` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the determination of the request or appeal has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(15): the decision, direction or other matter must be complied with` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the Act provides otherwise` THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `a reconsideration request or an appeal has been made under section 89` AND (NOT `the determination of the request or appeal has been made`)

-- src:6149 | (16) The Minister may make regulations in respect of the manner in
-- src:6150 | which an appeal may be made to the Minister under subsection (1),
-- src:6151 | (2) or (7) and the procedure to be adopted in hearing such appeals.
@ref s 89(16) (src:6149-6151)
GIVEN `the regulations are in respect of the manner in which an appeal may be made to the Minister under subsection (1), (2) or (7), or the procedure to be adopted in hearing such appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89(16): the Minister may make the regulations` MEANS
    `the regulations are in respect of the manner in which an appeal may be made to the Minister under subsection (1), (2) or (7), or the procedure to be adopted in hearing such appeals`

§ `s 90 Interest on sums unpaid`

-- src:6159 | 90. If any sum required to be paid by a telecommunication licensee
-- src:6160 | or a person granted a spectrum right under this Act or any code of
-- src:6161 | practice or regulation made under this Act is not paid when it is
-- src:6162 | required to be paid, that licensee or person is liable to pay the
-- src:6163 | Authority the prescribed interest on such unpaid sums for the period
-- src:6164 | such sums remain unpaid.
@ref s 90 (src:6159-6164)
GIVEN `the sum is required to be paid by a telecommunication licensee or a person granted a spectrum right under the Act, or under a code of practice or regulation made under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum is not paid when it is required to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90: the licensee or person is liable to pay the Authority the prescribed interest on the unpaid sum for the period it remains unpaid` MEANS
    `the sum is required to be paid by a telecommunication licensee or a person granted a spectrum right under the Act, or under a code of practice or regulation made under the Act` AND `the sum is not paid when it is required to be paid`
